  "strategy": "I'll implement a specialized step function optimization using continuous coordinate ascent through sequential convex programming. This approach will use the optimal sequence from the previous program as one initialization point and two geometric sequences generated by FFT-based gradient evaluation.\n\nApproach:\n1. We'll start from the best candidate of length 512 (if available) and perform a uphill-only coordinate ascent: increasing one coefficient at a time to minimize the objective function.\n\n2. We'll maintain a population of 4 diverse initial sequences:\n   - One normalized version of the provided parent sequence\n   - Two FFT-evolved sequences (chirp and multi-tone)\n   - One pure random sequence\n\n3. The core update procedure will:\n   a) Keep the best candidate so far\n   b) Attempt to increase each coefficient position one at a time, but only if it improves the objective\n   c) After successful updates, normalize the sequence (except the current coordinate) to maintain the required length (512)\n\n4. Evaluation:\n   - Use the original evaluate_sequence function to validate progress\n   - Absolute verbose logging at 5-minute intervals\n\nImplementation details:\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport time\nfrom scipy.optimize import minpack2  # Only if we need, but we're not using for this method\n\ndef resample_sequence(seq, new_n=512):\n    \"\"\"Resample sequence length to new_n via linear interpolation\"\"\"\n    x_old = np.linspace(0, 1, len(seq), endpoint=True)\n    x_new = np.linspace(0, 1, new_n, endpoint=True)\n    return np.interp(x_new, x_old, seq)\n\ndef coordinate_ascent_step(sequence, epsilon=0.1, max_iterations=100):\n    \"\"\"Execute a single coordinate ascent step\"\"\"\n    current_score = evaluate_sequence(sequence)\n    best_sequence = sequence.copy()\n    best_score = current_score\n    \n    n = len(sequence)\n    S = np.sqrt(2.0 * n)  # Normalization for the provided parent method\n    \n    # Gradual parameter update\n    for pos in range(n):\n        # \u521b\u5efa\u4e0d\u5305\u542b\u5f53\u524d\u4f4d\u7f6e\u7684\u526f\u672c\n        copy_seq = sequence.copy()\n        # \u5347\u9ad8\u53c2\u6570\n        copy_seq[pos] += epsilon\n        \n        # \u6b63\u4ea4\u5230\u539f\u59cb\u5e8f\u5217\u7a7a\u95f4\n        normalized_copy = S * copy_seq / np.sum(copy_seq)\n        \n        # \u68c0\u6d4b\u662f\u5426\u6539\u5584\n        new_score = evaluate_sequence(normalized_copy)\n        if new_score < best_score:\n            best_score = new_score\n            best_sequence = normalized_copy.copy()\n    \n    # \u6807\u5fd7\u4f55\u65f6\u9700\u8981\u6700\u7ec8\u8f93\u51fa\n    return best_sequence, best_score\n\ndef fft_convolve(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\u7ebf\u6027\u5377\u79ef\"\"\"\n    n = len(a)\n    m = len(b)\n    if n != m:  # If need uneven array lengths, adjust\n        b = np.pad(b, (0, n - m), 'constant') if m < n else np.pad(b, \nconst(0, m - n), 'constant')\n    fa = np.fft.rfft(a)\n    fb = np.fft.rfft(b)\n    return np.fft.irfft(fa * fb)[:n]\n\ndef extract_critical_points(conv_result):\n    \"\"\"\u63d0\u53d6\u5377\u79ef\u7ed3\u679c\u4e2d\u7684\u5173\u952e\u70b9\"\"\"\n    critical_point = np.argmax(conv_result)\n    return np.linspace(critical_point - 0.5, critical_point + 0.5, 10)\n\ndef fftevolution_acent(sequence, target_conv):\n    \"\"\"FFT-specific\u68af\u5ea6\u4f30\u8ba1\"\"\"\n    n = len(sequence)\n    conv = fft_convolve(sequence, sequence)\n    sig_score = max(conv) / np.sum(conv)**2  # \u7b80\u5316\u5206\u6570\n    \n    updates = np.zeros(n)\n    # \u5bf9\u534a\u5f84\u57280.5\u52301.5\u4e4b\u95f4\u7684\u5173\u952e\u70b9\u8fdb\u884c\u66f4\u65b0\n    for i in range(n):\n        updates[i] = -target_conv[i]\n    \n    return updates\n\ndef initial_geometric_sequence(rng, base_case=1.0, order=3):\n    \"\"\"\u521b\u5efa\u57fa\u7840\u51e0\u4f55\u5e8f\u5217\"\"\"\n    amsr_coins = []\n    for mag in [effect\uff1a\n- **\u6b63\u4ea4\u6027**\uff1a\u9009\u62e9\u5728\u51